=== Team changes ===
[[Hitech Grand Prix|Hitech]] ended their partnership with [[Toyota Gazoo Racing]] after one season, dropping the 'TGR' moniker from its name.<sup><nowiki>[</nowiki>[[Wikipedia:Belege|''citation needed'']]<nowiki>]</nowiki></sup>

=== Driver changes ===
Reigning teams' champions [[Invicta Racing]] have an all-new driver lineup as reigning drivers' champion [[Leonardo Fornaroli]] joined the [[McLaren F1 Team]] as a reserve driver and [[Roman Staněk]] left Formula 2 to join [[Kondo Racing]]'s Buzz MK Racing offshoot in [[2026 Super Formula Championship|Super Formula]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Murphy |first=Drew |date=2026-01-15 |title=McLaren confirm Leonardo Fornaroli as 2026 reserve driver in academy update |url=https://www.gpblog.com/en/news/mclaren-confirm-leonardo-fornaroli-as-2026-reserve-driver-in-academy-update |access-date=2026-01-16 |website=GPblog |language=en}}</ref><ref name="Staněk">{{Cite news|url=https://www.autosport.com/super-formula/news/f2-race-winner-stanek-makes-super-formula-switch-with-kondo-racing/10799383/|title=F2 race winner Stanek makes Super Formula switch with Kondo Racing|date=21 February 2026|access-date=21 February 2026|work=[[Autosport]]|last=Klein|first=Jamie}}</ref> Invicta signed [[2025 FIA Formula 3 Championship|2025 FIA Formula 3 Champion]] and [[Ferrari Driver Academy]] driver [[Rafael Câmara]] from [[Trident Motorsport|Trident]], and [[Joshua Dürksen]], who left AIX Racing after finishing the 2025 campaign ninth to join the team for his third season in the championship.<ref>{{Cite web |title=2025 Formula 3 Champion Rafael Câmara steps up to F2 with Invicta Racing|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/5EqLKOLpgVAm8ujP8FNlGq/2025-formula-3-champion-rafael-camara-steps-up-to-f2-with-invicta-racing |date=28 October 2025|access-date=28 October 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website |language=en}}</ref><ref name="DurksenInvicta" />

[[Hitech GP|Hitech]] saw [[Dino Beganovic]] move to DAMS Lucas Oil and [[Luke Browning]] leave the series to compete in Super Formula with Kondo Racing.<ref name="BeganovicDAMS"/><ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.williamsf1.com/articles/e585a9bc-289d-440e-9553-7dac715b4e73/luke-browning-atlassian-williams-f1-team-reserve-role-full-driver-academy-2026?cid=sm_twx_|title=Luke Browning secures Atlassian Williams F1 Team Reserve role as full Driver Academy line-up is announced|date=16 January 2026|access-date=16 January 2026|work=[[Williams F1 Team]]}}</ref> They signed [[Cadillac F1]] test driver [[Colton Herta]] for his Formula 2 debut. He moved over from the [[IndyCar Series]], where he won nine races over eight years and ended the 2025 season in seventh driving for [[Andretti Global]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Medland |first=Chris |date=2025-10-21 |title=Herta to race with Hitech in F2 {{!}} RACER |url=https://racer.com/2025/10/20/herta-to-race-with-hitech-in-f2 |access-date=2025-10-21 |website=racer.com |language=en}}</ref> The team also signed former [[2023 Super Formula Championship|Super Formula]] champion [[Ritomo Miyata]], who embarks on his third F2 campaign after coming 17th with [[ART Grand Prix]] in 2025.<ref name="Miyata">{{Cite web |title=Hitech announces Ritomo Miyata for 2026 FIA Formula 2 campaign| url=https://www.hitechgp.co.uk/hitech-announces-ritomo-miyata-for-2026-fia-formula-2-campaign/|date=8 December 2025|access-date=8 December 2025|website=[[Hitech GP]]|language=en}}</ref>

Campos Racing saw [[Pepe Martí]] graduate to [[2025–26 Formula E World Championship|Formula E]] with [[Cupra Racing|Cupra]] [[Kiro Race Co|Kiro]] ahead of the penultimate round of the 2025 season, and [[Arvid Lindblad]] graduate to [[2026 Formula One World Championship|Formula One]] with [[Racing Bulls]].<ref name="Marti">{{Cite web |date=21 October 2025 |title=Pepe Martí joins CUPRA KIRO for 2025/26 FIA Formula E season |url=https://kiroraceco.com/latest/pepe-mart-joins-cupra-kiro-for-202526-fia-formula-e-season |access-date=21 October 2025 |website=[[Kiro Race Co]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2 December 2025 |title=Our Driver Line-Up For 2026|url=https://www.visacashapprb.com/int-en/2026-driver-live-up-announcement|access-date=2 December 2025 |website=[[Racing Bulls]] |language=en}}</ref> 2025 FIA F3 runner-up and [[Red Bull Junior Team]] driver [[Nikola Tsolov]], who already replaced Martí for the final two rounds of the 2025 season, stayed with Campos for his full-season graduation.<ref>{{Cite web |date=16 September 2025 |title=Nikola Tsolov Graduates to FIA Formula 2 with Campos Racing in 2026 |url=https://www.camposracing.com/en/noticias/fia-f2/nikola-tsolov-graduates-to-fia-formula-2-with-campos-racing-in-2026 |access-date=16 September 2025 |website=[[Campos Racing]]}}</ref> He was joined by [[Noel León]], who also stepped up from FIA F3 after finishing the 2025 season in 17th driving for Prema Racing.<ref>{{Cite web |date=21 October 2025 |title=Noel León to Make FIA F2 Debut with Campos Racing in 2026 |url=https://www.camposracing.com/en/noticias/fia-f2/noel-leon-to-make-fia-f2-debut-with-campos-racing-in-2026 |access-date=21 October 2025 |website=[[Campos Racing]]}}</ref>

[[DAMS|DAMS Lucas Oil]] have a new lineup as [[Kush Maini]] moved to [[ART Grand Prix]] and [[Jak Crawford]] left the series to join the [[Aston Martin in Formula One|Aston Martin F1 Team]] as their third driver.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Jak Crawford confirmed as Aston Martin Aramco Third Driver for 2026|url=https://www.astonmartinf1.com/en-GB/news/announcement/jak-crawford-confirmed-as-aston-martin-aramco-third-driver-for-2026|date=28 October 2025 |access-date=28 October 2025 |website=Aston Martin F1}}</ref> [[Ferrari Driver Academy]] member [[Dino Beganovic]] returned to the team where he made his F2 debut in 2024 as he departed [[Hitech GP|Hitech]], with whom he finished seventh in 2025, and [[Roman Bilinski]] made his series debut after finishing eleventh in FIA F3 with [[Rodin Motorsport]].<ref name="BeganovicDAMS">{{Cite web |title=DINO BEGANOVIC IS CONFIRMED FOR 2026!|url=https://damslucasoil.com/2025/10/22/dino-beganovic-is-confirmed-for-2026/|date=21 October 2025 |access-date=22 October 2025 |website=[[DAMS]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Roman Bilinski steps up to Formula 2 with DAMS Lucas Oil for 2026|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/3RurcrjQJx9BsvQSUWTnAV/roman-bilinski-steps-up-to-formula-2-with-dams-lucas-oil-for-2026|date=25 November 2025 |access-date=25 November 2025 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website}}</ref>

[[Richard Verschoor]] left [[MP Motorsport]] after spending five seasons in the category to join [[Duqueine Team]] in the [[2026 European Le Mans Series|European Le Mans Series]]' LMP2 class.<ref>{{cite web |date=8 July 2025 |title=F2 leader Verschoor confirms this season will be his last |url=https://formulascout.com/f2-leader-verschoor-confirms-this-season-will-be-his-last |access-date=8 July 2025 |website=Formula Scout}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Klein |first=Jamie |date=2025-12-17 |title=Record 47-Car Provisional Full-Season Entry List Revealed – Sportscar365 |url=https://sportscar365.com/lemans/elms/record-47-car-provisional-full-season-entry-list-revealed/ |access-date=2025-12-17 |language=en-US}}</ref> His replacement was [[Gabriele Minì]], who finished his first full season in F2 in 13th driving for [[Prema Racing]].<ref name="Mini">{{Cite web|title=Minì picks MP Motorsport for second full-season attempt at FIA Formula 2 glory|url=https://www.mpmotorsport.com/news/mini-picks-mp-motorsport-for-second-full-season-attempt-at-fia-formula-2-glory|date=8 December 2025|access-date=8 December 2025|website=[[MP Motorsport]]|language=en}}</ref>

[[Prema Racing]] replaced MP-bound Minì with [[Aston Martin in Formula One#Driver development programme|Aston Martin junior]] driver [[Mari Boya]], who graduated from FIA F3 after finishing the 2025 season in third with [[Campos Racing]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Boya joins PREMA Racing for 2026 FIA Formula 2 season|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19658-promising-spaniard-step-up-to-rookie-f2-year|date=24 November 2025|access-date=24 November 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref>

[[Rodin Motorsport]] driver [[Amaury Cordeel]] left Formula 2 ahead of the final two rounds of the 2025 season to join [[Team WRT]] in the [[2026 GT World Challenge Europe|GT World Challenge Europe]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Goodwin |first=Graham |date=2026-02-16 |title=Team WRT Complete 2026 GT World Challenge Europe Roster |url=https://www.dailysportscar.com/2026/02/16/team-wrt-complete-2026-gt-world-challenge-europe-roster.html |access-date=2026-02-16 |website=www.dailysportscar.com |language=en-GB}}</ref> To replace him, the team signed [[Martinius Stenshorne]] for his full-season debut after he had already entered the Baku round of the 2025 season with [[Trident Motorsport|Trident]] before deputising for Cordeel during the final two rounds of 2025. He stepped up from FIA F3, where he came fifth in 2025 with [[Hitech GP|Hitech]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=1 October 2025|title=Martinius Stenshorne joins Rodin Motorsport for 2026 campaign|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/5WORxKNqxNTSXTiGgxiEu0/martinius-stenshorne-joins-rodin-motorsport-for-2026-campaign|access-date=1 October 2025|website=FIA Formula 2 Championship}}</ref>

[[ART Grand Prix]] saw [[Ritomo Miyata]] move to Hitech, while [[Victor Martins]] left Formula 2 after three seasons to join [[Alpine Endurance Team|Alpine]] for their [[2026 FIA World Endurance Championship|WEC Hypercar]] programme and the [[Williams F1 Team]] as a test and development driver.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Villemant |first=Thibaut |last2=Khorounzhiy |first2=Valentin |date=2026-01-12 |title=Long-time F1 hopeful joins Alpine WEC roster |url=https://www.the-race.com/endurance/wec-alpine-new-signing-2026-victor-martins-williams/ |access-date=2026-01-12 |website=The Race |language=en}}</ref> The team signed Thai driver [[Tasanapol Inthraphuvasak]], who finished seventh with [[Campos Racing]] in the 2025 FIA F3 season and already made his F2 debut in the 2025 season finale driving for Trident, and [[Kush Maini]], who joined ART for his fourth F2 season after finishing 16th in 2025 with DAMS.<ref>{{Cite web |date=18 November 2025 |title=Tasanapol Inthraphusak graduates to Formula 2 in 2026 |url=https://www.art-grandprix.com/en/tasanapol-inthraphusak-graduates-to-formula-2-in-2026/ |access-date=18 November 2025 |website=[[ART Grand Prix]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=9 December 2025 |title=ART Grand Prix sign Kush Maini for the 2026 Formula 2 season |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/7SAyy3pFmIDFHfZOmSPzW/art-grand-prix-sign-kush-maini-for-the-2026-formula-2-season|access-date=9 December 2025|website=FIA Formula 2 Championship}}</ref>

[[Joshua Dürksen]] left [[AIX Racing]] after two seasons of driving for the team, to join [[Invicta Racing]].<ref name="DurksenInvicta">{{Cite web |title=Invicta Racing sign Joshua Duerksen for the 2026 Formula 2 season |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/21FlttUecWTenudO2ynXx1/invicta-racing-sign-joshua-duerksen-for-the-2026-formula-2-season |access-date=2025-10-22 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website |language=en}}</ref> To replace him, AIX signed [[Emerson Fittipaldi Jr.]], who stepped up from [[Eurocup-3]], where he drove for MP Motorsport.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=7 September 2025|title=Emmo Fittipaldi to leap up to F2 with AIX Racing in 2026 |url=https://formulascout.com/emmo-fittipaldi-to-leap-up-to-f2-with-aix-racing-in-2026/132980 |access-date=7 September 2025|website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref>

[[Van Amersfoort Racing]] saw [[John Bennett (racing driver)|John Bennett]] move to [[Trident Motorsport|Trident]].<ref name="Bennett">{{Cite web |title=FIA F2, John Bennett to Contest the 2026 FIA F2 with Trident Motorsport|url=https://www.tridentmotorsport.com/en/news/fia-f2,-john-bennett-to-contest-the-2026-fia-f2-with-trident-motorsport.html|date=9 December 2025|access-date=9 December 2025|website=[[Trident Motorsport]]|language=en}}</ref> [[2023 FIA World Endurance Championship|2023 FIA WEC LMGTE Am]] Champion and 24 Hours of Le Mans winner [[Nico Varrone]], who last competed in single-seaters in the [[2020 BRDC British Formula 3 Championship]], replaced him.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Van Amersfoort Racing welcomes Argentinian driver Nicolas Varrone to 2026 FIA Formula 2 campaign for 2026 |url=https://www.vanamersfoortracing.nl/news/2025/van-amersfoort-racing-welcomes-argentinian-driver-nicolas-varrone-to-2026-fia-formula-2-campaign/ |date=23 October 2025|access-date=23 October 2025|website=[[Van Amersfoort Racing]]|language=en}}</ref>

[[Trident Motorsport|Trident]] have an all-new lineup as [[Max Esterson]] and [[Sami Meguetounif]], who raced for the majority of 2025, did not return to the series, with Esterson joining [[Rahal Letterman Lanigan Racing|RLL Team McLaren]] in [[2026 IMSA SportsCar Championship|IMSA's GTD class]], and Meguetounif  joining [[TDS Racing]] in the European Le Mans Series' LMP2 class.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://sportscar365.com/imsa/iwsc/61-car-rolex-24-entry-list-released/|title=61-Car Rolex 24 Entry List Released|website=Sportscar365|publisher=John Dagys Media|last=Dagys|first=John|date=December 9, 2025|access-date=December 9, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.endurance-info.com/auto/article/119528-tds-racing-mise-sur-meguetounif-et-huffaker-pour-epauler-thomas-en-lmp2-pro-am|title=TDS Racing mise sur Meguetounif et Huffaker pour épauler Thomas en LMP2 Pro-Am|website=Endurance-Info|language=fr|date=8 March 2026|access-date=8 March 2026}}</ref> The team signed [[John Bennett (racing driver)|John Bennett]], who finished his debut F2 season 22nd with [[Van Amersfoort Racing]], and FIA F3 driver [[Laurens van Hoepen]], who came 12th with [[ART Grand Prix]] and already raced with Trident for the last three rounds of 2025.<ref name="Bennett"/><ref>{{Cite web |title=Van Hoepen to compete in the 2026 FIA F2 Championship with Trident|url=https://www.tridentmotorsport.com/en/news/van-hoepen-to-compete-in-the-2026-fia-f2-championship-with-trident.html|date=8 December 2025|access-date=8 December 2025|website=[[Trident Motorsport]]|language=en}}</ref>

